item.stdout:
{
  "command": "entire checkpoint explain",
  "short": "Explain a session, commit, or checkpoint",
  "long": "Explain provides human-readable context about sessions, commits, and checkpoints.\n\nUse this command to understand what happened during agent-driven development,\neither for self-review or to understand a teammate's work.\n\nBy default, shows checkpoints on the current branch. Pass a checkpoint ID or\ncommit SHA as a positional argument to explain a specific item, or use flags.\n\nViewing specific items:\n  entire checkpoint explain \u003cid-or-sha\u003e           Auto-detects checkpoint ID or commit SHA\n  entire checkpoint explain --checkpoint \u003cid\u003e     Force interpretation as checkpoint ID\n  entire checkpoint explain --commit \u003cref\u003e        Force interpretation as commit ref\n\nCheckpoints in another repo:\n  entire checkpoint explain \u003cid\u003e --repo owner/name\n                 Explain a checkpoint owned by another repository — the\n                 drill-down for a cross-repo 'entire search' hit. Reads it from\n                 that repo's Entire API; nothing is written to this repo.\n                 Needs a full checkpoint ID (positional or --checkpoint) and a\n                 checkpoint that has been pushed.\n\nFiltering the list view:\n  --session      Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n\nOutput verbosity levels (when explaining a specific item):\n  Default:         Detailed view with scoped prompts (ID, session, tokens, intent, prompts, files)\n  --short          Summary only (ID, session, timestamp, tokens, intent)\n  --full           Parsed full transcript (all prompts/responses from entire session)\n  --raw-transcript Raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n\nMachine-readable export modes (additive surface for external consumers):\n  --json           Metadata-only JSON. Lists checkpoints when no target is given;\n                   emits a single checkpoint envelope when a target is supplied.\n                   Transcript bytes are NEVER embedded in the JSON envelope.\n  --transcript     Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes (JSONL) to stdout\n                   for the selected session. Same bytes as --raw-transcript\n                   while checkpoints v1 is the checkpoint store.\n  --session-index  Pick a session within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based).\n                   Defaults to the latest session. Only meaningful with\n                   --transcript or --raw-transcript.\n  --limit          Cap the number of checkpoints returned by the list view.\n                   Defaults to 100. When the cap is hit, a stderr note\n                   says how many were skipped. Only meaningful with --json.\n\nSummary generation:\n  --generate    Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint\n  --force       Regenerate even if a summary already exists (requires --generate)\n\nPerformance options:\n  --search-all  Remove branch/depth limits when searching for commits (may be slow)\n\nCheckpoint detail view shows:\n  - Author of the checkpoint\n  - Associated git commits that reference the checkpoint\n  - Prompts and responses from the session\n\nNote: --session filters the list view; the positional arg, --commit, and --checkpoint are mutually exclusive.",
  "repo": "gh/MuskanPaliwal/cli",
  "flags": [
    {
      "name": "checkpoint",
      "shorthand": "c",
      "type": "string",
      "usage": "Explain a specific checkpoint (ID or prefix)"
    },
    {
      "name": "commit",
      "type": "string",
      "usage": "Explain a specific commit (SHA or ref, \"commit-ish\")"
    },
    {
      "name": "force",
      "type": "bool",
      "default": "false",
      "usage": "Regenerate summary even if one already exists (requires --generate)"
    },
    {
      "name": "full",
      "type": "bool",
      "default": "false",
      "usage": "Show full parsed transcript (all prompts/responses)"
    },
    {
      "name": "generate",
      "type": "bool",
      "default": "false",
      "usage": "Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint"
    },
    {
      "name": "insecure-http-auth",
      "type": "bool",
      "default": "false",
      "usage": "Allow plain-HTTP auth for --repo (local dev only)"
    },
    {
      "name": "json",
      "type": "bool",
      "default": "false",
      "usage": "Output metadata as JSON (no transcript bytes)"
    },
    {
      "name": "limit",
      "type": "int",
      "default": "0",
      "usage": "Cap the list view at N checkpoints (default: 100). Only meaningful with --json."
    },
    {
      "name": "no-pager",
      "type": "bool",
      "default": "false",
      "usage": "Disable pager output"
    },
    {
      "name": "raw-transcript",
      "type": "bool",
      "default": "false",
      "usage": "Show raw transcript file (JSONL format)"
    },
    {
      "name": "repo",
      "type": "string",
      "usage": "Explain a checkpoint owned by another repo (owner/name or gh/owner/name), read from that repo's Entire API"
    },
    {
      "name": "search-all",
      "type": "bool",
      "default": "false",
      "usage": "Search all commits (no branch/depth limit, may be slow)"
    },
    {
      "name": "session",
      "type": "string",
      "usage": "Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)"
    },
    {
      "name": "session-index",
      "type": "int",
      "default": "-1",
      "usage": "Session index within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based, defaults to latest)"
    },
    {
      "name": "short",
      "shorthand": "s",
      "type": "bool",
      "default": "false",
      "usage": "Show summary only (omit prompts and files)"
    },
    {
      "name": "summary-timeout-seconds",
      "type": "int",
      "default": "0",
      "usage": "Hard deadline in seconds for --generate summary generation; overrides summary_timeout_seconds setting. 0 = use setting; if setting is also unset or 0, no automatic deadline applies."
    },
    {
      "name": "transcript",
      "type": "bool",
      "default": "false",
      "usage": "Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes to stdout"
    },
    {
      "name": "context",
      "type": "string",
      "usage": "Act as this saved login `name` for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)"
    }
  ]
}

